Z||000000||Shawn85SE||03-19-2000||11:09 AM||||The radio in my SE is just about dead. It will work for about 15 minutes then just quit. Its the high end model and I really like it. I was just wondering if anyone else had this problem? And if so whats the fix? If all else fails what radio from other cars will fit? Its a long drive to work without music. thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||03-19-2000||01:33 PM||||I have one of those sterios too... all push-button and has the 5 band EQ. The button that you push to turn up the volume doesn't work. Anyone know how to fix that?||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||03-19-2000||03:15 PM||||I took my radio to the Pontiac dealer to see what i would cost to repair.  Display doesn't work and a couple of buttons acting up.  Estimate was $300.00.  I went to a flea market and picked up an aftermarket radio untill the money fairy visits.  I found a place on the web to hook up a relay so I could use my factory sub  but that was after I burned out the power antenna circuit on the new radio.  Some creative wiring and a dash switch from a car with rear window defog and now I can use the sub.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-19-2000||03:36 PM||||You could get a Pontiac up3 with cd player. I know it is not factory but it looks it. It lights up the same color as the rest of the dash. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/radio.JPG"> <BR>The only thing I had to do was go to pontiac and get a $20 adapter that makes the radio plug in to the fiero harness perfectly. I love it. if your interested here is a link to the site I got it from. <A HREF="http://www.aatechnologies.com/pmyradios/pontiac/16205302.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.aatechnologies.com/pmyradios/pontiac/16205302.asp</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||03-19-2000||04:54 PM||||I got to say that UP3 model is a nice looking piece!<P>Since the only CDs I have, have software on them, no music, I am looking for a radio that I can play my cassettes and 8 tracks on!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Or a VCR that will play my BETA tapes, or ...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Paul<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000005||Poncho Jim||03-19-2000||08:44 PM||||The UP3 was available on early to mid 90's Grand Am cars and TransPort vans.  I plugged one into my 90 Trans Am to be able to play CD's and keep the stock look.  (Aftermarket players with red lighting are hard to come by).<P>They do make a cassette version of the radio..  UP(something) If you browse a few boneyards, you should be able to pick up a cassette model at a decent price.  New, they're around 250 bucks.<P>BTW, they do AM stereo which you might appreciate if they have a decent station in your area broadcasting in AM stereo.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||03-19-2000||08:53 PM||||I went the aftermarket route. I have a Pioneer DEH-P86DHR It's AM/FM/CD with 25wX4 speaker output and a subwoofer controling output. It also has CD naming and Radio station ID Display. (displays radio call sign and music type) The face plate is removable and it has a small remote control that fits perfect in the gap on a 4-spoke steering wheel! If I want to I can add a CD changer too!||||reg||1
Z||000007||phillip||03-19-2000||09:18 PM||||i never considered keeping the factory radio.i lucked across a jvc 3 cd indash changer/radio (sears was clearing them out for $250).i have a 1/2 din eq in the dash with it (profile).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||03-19-2000||09:27 PM||||  Shawn, The cassette version is the UX1, it too was in the Grand Prix. It is listed on the above mentioned site with the link. Click on the pontiac ICON and your there <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  BAM-OUT! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
